Dear Kellan,

Thank you for your report on the visit to 16 Brindlewick Mews today. Please do not open up the ceiling lining, drill or carry out any repair for now. Only the inspection visit has been requested, and any opening-up or repair needs the landlord's separate approval.

Please send us a quote covering:
- the limited opening in the ceiling lining needed to reach the compression joint, and any making good afterwards;
- the repair to the joint;
- the complete all-inclusive total, stating whether VAT is included;
- the earliest date you could do the work.

Once we have the quote we will ask the landlord for approval and let you know the answer.

Kind regards,
Northbridge Lettings

Dear Kellan,

Thank you for your estimate for 16 Brindlewick Mews (isolating the pipe, opening about 30 cm of ceiling lining, replacing the joint and making the opening safe).

The estimate we received does not show a figure we can pass to the landlord. Please confirm:
- the complete total for the work described, and whether VAT is included;
- whether making good the ceiling finish (filling and decorating) is included or excluded;
- the earliest date you could do the work;
- what the exclusion for investigation, testing, removal and disposal of suspect material refers to. Did you see anything that you suspect, and if so, what, and could it add cost or change the scope?

Please do not start any work, open the ceiling or drill. Only the inspection visit has been requested so far. The repair needs the landlord's separate approval, and we will tell you as soon as we have their answer.

Kind regards,
Northbridge Lettings
